IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- THE 2001 TEXT.  The Regulations as made (S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001) are deposited and compared with the 2002 Revised Edition regulation by regulation in sgta-i-rg5-as-made.l4
-- (59 of the 80 regulations have the same words).  A function below that takes a date starts on 2 March 2001 where the regulation it encodes has the same words as made (regs 24, 57, 64, 65, 78),
-- differs only in the order of its paragraphs (reg 20), or did not yet exist (reg 65A: FALSE until S 461/2009); reg 76 answers with its as-made wording before 1 January 2003.
-- Functions of the other sibling modules that take no date answer on the Revised Edition's words; the comparison table says, regulation by regulation, whether those are the 2001 words.

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), made by the Authority with the
-- Minister's approval under section 74 of the Telecommunications Act (section 97 in the 2020 Revised Edition).
-- Texts used, all deposited under subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/:
--   TA1999-RG5 (the 2002 Revised Edition) and the amending regulations TA1999-RG5-S707-2005, -S263-2006, -S461-2009, -S20-2011, -S100-2016.
--
-- WHAT IS IN THIS FILE (the provisions on possessing, using and licensing a station): reg 2 "station", reg 19(1) (when a
-- station may be possessed or operated), reg 65 and 65A (the class licences), reg 78 (which breaches are offences).
-- The rest of Rg 5 is in the sibling modules: sgta-i-rg5-spectrum.l4 (Parts II and III), sgta-i-rg5-licences.l4 (Parts IV to VII),
-- sgta-i-rg5-duties.l4 (Parts IX and X), sgta-i-rg5-schedules.l4 (the Schedules) and sgta-i-rg5-amendments.l4 (what each amending instrument changes).
--
-- VINTAGES.  Before 1 January 2003 -> NOTHING: the 2002 Revised Edition's start date is not printed in the PDF and the
-- earlier text is not deposited.  The windows below are cut at the commencement dates of the amendments that touch the
-- modelled provisions: 1 June 2006 (S 263/2006 adds a sixth public system to reg 65(4)), 2 October 2009 (S 461/2009
-- adds "other than a telecommunication licensee", renames the licence and adds reg 65A) and 1 April 2016 (S 100/2016
-- changes the list in reg 78).
-- The last amendment on IMDA's listing is S 100/2016; the listing may not be current, so a later amendment is unknown.

§ `Rg 5 regulation 2: station`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:273 | "station" means a transmitter, a receiver, a combination of transmitters and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:274 | receivers or any accessory thereto which is used or intended to be used for
-- src:TA1999-RG5:275 | radio-communication;
@ref Rg 5 reg 2 "station" (src:TA1999-RG5:273-275)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
      `it is an accessory to a transmitter or a receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2: the equipment is a station` MEANS
        (   elem `reception` (e's `acts it is used or intended to be used for`)
         OR elem `transmission` (e's `acts it is used or intended to be used for`)
         OR elem `emission` (e's `acts it is used or intended to be used for`)
         OR `it is an accessory to a transmitter or a receiver`)
    AND elem `Hertzian or radio waves` (e's `means it uses`)

§ `Rg 5 regulation 19: licensing requirement`

-- Regulation 19(1) says when a station "may be possessed, established, installed, maintained, provided or operated".
-- It is a permission in form ("may ... if authorised by"); it is not an offence provision, and reg 78 does not list it.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:555 | 19. —(1) A station or network may be possessed, established, installed, maintained,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:556 | provided or operated if authorised by —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:557 | (a) a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:558 | (b) a station licence or network licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:559 | (c) a class licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 19(1) (src:TA1999-RG5:555-559)
GIVEN `holds a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holds a station licence or network licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holds a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 19(1): the station may be possessed, established, installed, maintained, provided or operated` MEANS
        `holds a station (spectrum) licence or network (spectrum) licence`
    OR `holds a station licence or network licence`
    OR `holds a class licence`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 65: class licences`

-- 2002 Revised Edition form: five public systems.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1094 | 65. —(1) A person who possesses or uses a relevant radio-communication station shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1095 | be deemed to have been granted a class licence by the Authority for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1101 | (a) a public cellular mobile telephone system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1102 | (b) a public radio paging system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1103 | (c) a public mobile data system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1104 | (d) a public trunked radio system;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1105 | (e) a public satellite mobile telephone or data system,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1106 | and includes a radio-communication station that is capable of being used in connection
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1107 | with any of the telecommunication systems referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) to (e) but
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1108 | which is not in use and not so connected.
@ref Rg 5 reg 65(1) and (4), 2002 Revised Edition (src:TA1999-RG5:1094-1108)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Public system of Rg 5 reg 65(4)`
`Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, 2002 Revised Edition` MEANS
    LIST `a public cellular mobile telephone system`
       , `a public radio paging system`
       , `a public mobile data system`
       , `a public trunked radio system`
       , `a public satellite mobile telephone or data system`

-- S 263/2006, from 1 June 2006: a sixth system, "a public wireless broadband access system".
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:14 | 1. —(1) These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:15 | communication) (Amendment) Regulations 2006 and shall, with the exception of regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:16 | 6 and 10, come into operation on 1st June 2006.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:17 | (2) Regulations 6 and 10 shall be deemed to have come into operation on 1st May 2006.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:77 | 8. Regulation 65 (4) of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:78 | (a) by deleting the comma at the end of sub-paragraph (e) and substituting a semi-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:79 | colon, and by inserting immediately thereafter the following sub-paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:80 | “(f) a public wireless broadband access system,”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:81 | (b) by deleting the words “sub-paragraphs (a) to (e)” in the penultimate line and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:82 | substituting the words “sub-paragraphs (a) to (f)”.
@ref Rg 5 reg 65(4) as amended by S 263/2006 (src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:14-17; src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:77-82)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Public system of Rg 5 reg 65(4)`
`Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, from 1 June 2006` MEANS
    append `Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, 2002 Revised Edition` (LIST `a public wireless broadband access system`)

-- S 461/2009, from 2 October 2009: "A person, other than a telecommunication licensee, ..." and "an individual station
-- class licence"; new reg 65A for telecommunication licensees' Fourth Schedule stations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:17 | (Amendment) Regulations 2009 and shall come into operation on 2nd October 2009.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:53 | 5. Regulation 65 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:54 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “A person” in paragraph (1), the words “,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:55 | other than a telecommunication licensee,”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:56 | (b) by deleting the words “a class licence” in paragraphs (1) and (3) and substituting in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:57 | each case the words “an individual station class licence”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:58 | (c) by deleting the words “A class licence” in paragraph (2) and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:59 | “An individual station class licence”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:60 | (d) by deleting the regulation heading and substituting the following regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:61 | heading:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:63 | “Grant of individual station class licences”.
@ref Rg 5 reg 65 as amended by S 461/2009 (src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:16-17; src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:53-63)
-- The rule starts on 2 March 2001, the day the Regulations as made (S 114/2001) came into operation: regulation 65 of S 114/2001 has the same words as the 2002 Revised Edition's (sgta-i-rg5-as-made.l4,
-- `Rg 5 as made (S 114/2001): the words of the regulation are those of the 2002 Revised Edition` "65"), and none of S 339/2001, S 374/2001 and S 450/2001 amends it (they amend the First Schedule, reg 26(4) and reg 28(1)).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `possesses or uses a station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system the station is connected with, if any` IS A MAYBE `Public system of Rg 5 reg 65(4)`
      `it is capable of being used with such a system but is not in use and not so connected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 65: the person is deemed granted the class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN
               JUST (`possesses or uses a station`
                     AND (   `it is capable of being used with such a system but is not in use and not so connected`
                          OR (CONSIDER `the system the station is connected with, if any`
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST sys THEN elem sys (`Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, 2002 Revised Edition`))))
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN
               JUST (`possesses or uses a station`
                     AND (   `it is capable of being used with such a system but is not in use and not so connected`
                          OR (CONSIDER `the system the station is connected with, if any`
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST sys THEN elem sys (`Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, from 1 June 2006`))))
           OTHERWISE
               JUST (`possesses or uses a station`
                     AND (NOT `is a telecommunication licensee`)
                     AND (   `it is capable of being used with such a system but is not in use and not so connected`
                          OR (CONSIDER `the system the station is connected with, if any`
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST sys THEN elem sys (`Rg 5 reg 65(4): the public systems, from 1 June 2006`))))

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:66 | 6. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after regulation 65, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:67 | following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:69 | “Grant of station (spectrum) class licences
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:70 | 65A.—(1) A telecommunication licensee who operates a radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:71 | specified in the Fourth Schedule shall be deemed to have been granted a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:72 | (spectrum) class licence by the Authority for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:73 | (2) A station (spectrum) class licence shall be subject to the conditions specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:74 | Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:75 | (3) No fee is payable for the grant of a station (spectrum) class licence.”.
@ref Rg 5 reg 65A inserted by S 461/2009 (src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:66-75)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `is a telecommunication licensee operating a station specified in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 65A: the person is deemed granted a station (spectrum) class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST `is a telecommunication licensee operating a station specified in the Fourth Schedule`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the conditions in the Fifth Schedule are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 65A(2): the station (spectrum) class licensee is within the station (spectrum) class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the conditions in the Fifth Schedule are met`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 65A(3): the fee payable for the grant of a station (spectrum) class licence in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST 0

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person contravenes a direction or notice of the Authority issued under regulation 74` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 78(b): contravening a direction or notice issued under regulation 74 is an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the person contravenes a direction or notice of the Authority issued under regulation 74`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 78: offence`

-- 2002 Revised Edition list.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1260 | 78. Any person who —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1261 | (a) contravenes regulation 24, 31, 32, 33, 35 (2), 36, 54, 56 (2), 57, 63 (1), (2) or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1262 | (3), 64, 67, 68, 69 or 70; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1263 | (b) contravenes any direction or notice of the Authority issued under regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1264 | 74,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1265 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 78, 2002 Revised Edition (src:TA1999-RG5:1260-1265)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 5 reg 78(a): the regulations whose breach is an offence, 2002 Revised Edition` MEANS
    LIST "24", "31", "32", "33", "35(2)", "36", "54", "56(2)", "57", "63(1)", "63(2)", "63(3)", "64", "67", "68", "69", "70"

-- S 100/2016, from 1 April 2016.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:21 | 1. These Regulations are the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:22 | (Radio-communication) (Amendment) Regulations 2016 and come
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:23 | into operation on 1 April 2016.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:175 | 13. Regulation 78 of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:176 | deleting paragraph (a) and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:177 | “(a) contravenes regulation 24(1), 31, 32, 33, 35(2), 36, 54, 56(2),
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:178 | 63(1), (2) or (3), 67, 68, 69 or 70; or”.
@ref Rg 5 reg 78(a) as substituted by S 100/2016 (src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:21-23; src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:175-178)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Rg 5 reg 78(a): the regulations whose breach is an offence, from 1 April 2016` MEANS
    LIST "24(1)", "31", "32", "33", "35(2)", "36", "54", "56(2)", "63(1)", "63(2)", "63(3)", "67", "68", "69", "70"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `regulation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 78(a): breach of this regulation is an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN JUST (elem `regulation` (`Rg 5 reg 78(a): the regulations whose breach is an offence, 2002 Revised Edition`))
           OTHERWISE JUST (elem `regulation` (`Rg 5 reg 78(a): the regulations whose breach is an offence, from 1 April 2016`))
